      <marc:subfield code="a">The Roman Arena, with its cruel and bloody games, remains one of the greatest mysteries of the Ancient world. For over five hundred years, lethal gladiatorial contests, staged to enetertain the Empires&apos; privileged classes, dominated Roman society. Wild beast hunts, reconstructured battles fought with deadly weapons and mass executions of prisoners were an integral part of these increasingly lavish spectacles.</marc:subfield>
